6.Which attribute is used to specify that an element is not yet relevant and should not be rendered
A)hide
B)invisible
C)hidden//answer


✅ Correct Answer: C. hidden

Explanation (Simple)

The hidden attribute tells the browser that an element is not relevant or should not be displayed.

Example:
<p hidden>This text is hidden.</p>

The paragraph exists in the HTML but is not rendered (not shown) by the browser.

Why not the others?
❌ A. hide → Not a valid HTML attribute.
❌ B. invisible → Not a valid HTML attribute.
✅ C. hidden → Correct! Hides the element from being rendered.
❌ D. (No valid option shown.)

✅ Correct Answer: C. hidden

